	<h2>Projects</h2>

	
	<article>

		
			
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Where do projects come from?</h3>


<div class="wp-block-image is-resized">
<figure class="alignright size-medium"><a href="https://uvision.utah.gov/"><img decoding="async" src="/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/UtahTransportationVision-300x63.jpg" alt="Utah's Transportation Vision: Pathway to Quality of Life" class="wp-image-12059"/></a></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">By the time citizens see construction equipment and orange barrels local governments and transit agencies, planning organizations, and the Utah Department of Transportation UDOT have been developing the visions and plans that led to the project for many years. The process begins with <a href="https://uvision.utah.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Utah&#8217;s Transportation Vision</a> which involves collaboration with partnering agencies, for example cities, to establish a shared vision for transportation statewide.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="alignleft size-medium"><a href="https://unifiedplan.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img decoding="async" src="/wp-content/uploads/2020/06/Unified-Transportation-Plan-300x93.png" alt="Utah's Unified Transportation Plan" class="wp-image-12072"/></a></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This vision is then used by planning organizations, Utah Transit Authority (UTA) and the Utah Department of Transportation (UDOT) to develop <a href="https://unifiedplan.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Utah&#8217;s Unified Transportation Plan</a>. This process involves these partners working together to develop common goals as well as plan time horizons, performance measures and financial assumptions. Everyone then agrees on which projects and needs to include in the Unified Plan, as well as timing, funding and how to measure their effectiveness in meeting shared objectives.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The <a href="/about-us/commission/">Utah Transportation Commission</a> uses the <a href="https://unifiedplan.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Unified Transportation Plan</a> to begin the <a href="/about-us/commission/project-prioritization-process/">Project Prioritization Process</a> and assign funds. This results in the <a href="/about-us/commission/stip/">Statewide Transportation Improvement Plan (STIP)</a>. The STIP is a six year plan of highway and transit projects throughout Utah and the Utah Department of Transportation (UDOT) uses this as a work plan for future studies and projects.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity"/>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For details on how active projects are currently impacting Utah roads, check out <a href="https://udottraffic.utah.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UDOT Traffic</a>.</p>



